{"availability":"available","full":"ZikangLeng/IMUGPT","name":"IMUGPT","description":"Generate virtual IMU data from text using LLMs and motion synthesis (ISWC 2023 Best Paper Honorable Mention; IMWUT 2024)","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Tcl","stars":49,"forks":8,"created":"2023-07-15T13:45:11Z","updated":"2026-10-09T15:55:46Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://zikangleng.github.io/imugpt/","topics":["human-activity-recognition","imu","llm","motion-generation","synthetic-data","wearable-sensing"],"demo":"https://zikangleng.github.io/imugpt/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T21:31:44.890Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T21:31:44.890Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T21:31:44.890Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T23:19:56.210Z","stars":49,"forks":8},{"at":"2026-10-16T21:31:44.890Z","stars":49,"forks":8}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Zikang Leng, Amitrajit Bhattacharjee, Hrudhai Rajasekhar, Lizhe Zhang, Elizabeth Bruda, Hyeokhyen Kwon, Thomas Plötz","Generated with IMUGPT: GPT-written activity descriptions → T2M-GPT motion → virtual accelerometer at the forearm (orange dot).","Labelled wearable data is scarce and expensive to collect. IMUGPT generates it from language:"],"features":["A large language model writes many diverse descriptions of an activity.","A text-to-motion model turns each description into 3D human motion.","The motion is converted into virtual on-body IMU data that trains human activity recognition (HAR) models.","IMUGPT (ISWC 2023, Best Paper Honorable Mention) introduced the language → motion → virtual IMU pipeline. Adding virtual data improved a Random Forest on all three benchmarks:","On RealWorld, the virtual-only model beats the real-only one using under an hour of generated motion."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ZikangLeng/IMUGPT/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8e958349b01c7717288fe2613640a4d92741570482c86682e74105c5cbe119ba","extra